WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.890
Release a ball from rest, and let it
speed up steadily down a long ramp.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.790
Record how far it has gone at each moment.

3
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.240
Plot displacement against time.

4
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.680
You get a curve.

5
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.640
The law is in there, but hard to read.

6
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:18.250
A straight line is easy: a
gradient and an intercept.

7
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.990
So how can a straight line expose
a law hiding inside a curve?

8
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.680
In this mission, you'll
draw graphs properly,

9
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.910
and read gradients, intercepts
and areas, with units.

10
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.680
Then you'll send a ball past a
row of electronic timing gates,

11
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.630
and pull its acceleration and
starting speed from one line.

12
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: find out how a straight
line can reveal a law hidden in a curve.
